WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:22.676
At night, while the others slept, the Little Mermaid went up to the palace balcony.

2
00:00:22.677 --> 00:00:28.260
From there she watched the waves and remembered her family beneath the sea.

3
00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:34.129
One night she saw her sisters swimming in the waves far away.

4
00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:39.279
"We miss our dear little sister," the oldest cried out.

5
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:42.543
She, of course, could not reply.

6
00:00:42.544 --> 00:00:46.508
Instead she thought, "I miss you too.

7
00:00:46.509 --> 00:00:51.573
But I will marry my Prince and live happily in the Upper World."

8
00:00:51.574 --> 00:00:55.795
When she waved to her sisters, they recognized her.

9
00:00:55.796 --> 00:00:59.338
They swam closer, up to the rocks.

10
00:00:59.339 --> 00:01:04.466
She held out her arms, to show them she would hug them if she could.

11
00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:10.744
From then on they came almost every night to sing to their sister.

12
00:01:10.745 --> 00:01:17.862
Once she even saw the Wise Mermaid, who had not been up to the surface in many years.

13
00:01:17.863 --> 00:01:21.728
With her grandmother was her father, the Sea King.

14
00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:27.709
They stretched out their hands to her, but they did not come as close as her sisters.

15
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:34.256
Her grandmother seemed to be saying, "We miss you, our dear child."

16
00:01:34.257 --> 00:01:39.836
But the Little Mermaid still wanted a soul and to be with the Prince.

17
00:01:39.837 --> 00:01:44.770
"I love seeing the world with you, little companion," the Prince would say.

18
00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.516
"You are very dear to me."

19
00:01:47.517 --> 00:01:51.876
Yet he never suggested making her his bride.

20
00:01:51.877 --> 00:01:54.545
"He sees me as his friend.

21
00:01:54.546 --> 00:01:59.206
But I need to be his wife," the Little Mermaid thought.

22
00:01:59.207 --> 00:02:04.681
"And if he marries someone else, I will turn into foam on the waves."

23
00:02:04.682 --> 00:02:09.421
She shivered thinking about such a fate.

24
00:02:09.422 --> 00:02:17.187
Sometimes the Little Mermaid begged the Prince with her eyes, "Please love me best of all.

25
00:02:17.188 --> 00:02:20.066
Love me enough to marry me."

26
00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:25.225
When she looked at him that way, the Prince would take her in his arms.

27
00:02:25.226 --> 00:02:29.904
He'd kiss her lightly on her forehead, in a brotherly way.

28
00:02:29.905 --> 00:02:34.516
But the Little Mermaid hoped that this would change.

29
00:02:34.517 --> 00:02:38.148
One day the Queen announced to her husband,

30
00:02:38.149 --> 00:02:41.646
"It is time for the Prince to marry."

31
00:02:41.647 --> 00:02:46.170
She wanted him to marry a princess from a neighboring kingdom.

32
00:02:46.171 --> 00:02:50.317
"Let's arrange for them to meet," she told him.

33
00:02:50.318 --> 00:02:54.153
When the Prince heard about this, he shook his head.

34
00:02:54.154 --> 00:02:58.661
"I will never marry that princess, little companion," he said.

35
00:02:58.662 --> 00:03:02.255
"I can only marry the one I truly love."

36
00:03:02.256 --> 00:03:05.809
Then he told the Little Mermaid his story.

37
00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:10.118
"Once I was on a ship that sank, and I almost drowned.

38
00:03:10.119 --> 00:03:13.287
Luckily I was swept ashore.

39
00:03:13.288 --> 00:03:17.780
When I opened my eyes, I saw the girl who had saved my life.

40
00:03:17.781 --> 00:03:22.249
Her name is Maiden, and she brought me inside a nearby church.

41
00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.662
When I awoke the next day, she was gone.

42
00:03:25.663 --> 00:03:30.759
Though I saw her only once, that girl is the only person I would wed.

43
00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.622
Unless I find her, I will never marry."

44
00:03:34.623 --> 00:03:39.337
"But it was I who saved you!" thought the Little Mermaid.

45
00:03:39.338 --> 00:03:41.962
"Please try to understand."

46
00:03:41.963 --> 00:03:47.027
But the Prince could not understand and only smiled at her.

47
00:03:47.028 --> 00:03:51.287
"Oh, little companion, do not feel sad because of my story.

48
00:03:51.288 --> 00:03:56.193
Even though I will never find her, I am happy with you by my side."

49
00:03:56.194 --> 00:04:00.404
"If only he knew the truth," she thought.

50
00:04:00.405 --> 00:04:05.950
"Someday the Prince will realize that I love him more than anyone does.

51
00:04:05.951 --> 00:04:09.683
And in time he will marry me."

52
00:04:09.684 --> 00:04:21.498
She would have to be patient for a little while longer.
